      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T09:25:00Z",
      "note": "The exploit is one transaction whose entry contract is created inside it and calls the executor\u2019s printMoney() seven times, once per token; each call reaches the holder contract, which performs the ERC-20 transfer to the attacker EOA. keccak of printMoney() is 0x94655f2b, matching the selector named in the snapshot summary. The executor is not upgradeable: its runtime code hash is identical at the deployment block 52031002 and at block 52052679 and its EIP-1967 implementation slot is zero, so the exploited code is 9 hours 2 minutes old. Its deployer 0xb6f90981027b95d74b58cb728672bc0143400ad0 is not the attacker. The defect is placed on the executor rather than the holder because the holder\u2019s transfer entry point does restrict its caller to the executor; the missing check is printMoney()\u2019s. The v1 loss figure of USD 2,000,000 is not reproducible: the holder\u2019s entire balance at the exploit block, and the attacker\u2019s entire gain, is USD 35,145.31."
    }
  ],
